			"notes": "# Comet 0.27.0\n\nFor Minecraft **26.2**, **26.1.2** and **1.21.11**. Released 28 October 2026.\n\nThis is the first release since **0.25.20** (23 October 2026). It includes all the work from versions 0.26.25 to 0.26.27, which were never published on their own, so everything below is new if you're coming from 0.25.20.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### Highway Fly (new)\n\nOne **highway-fly** module for long elytra trips along the highways:\n\n- **Flight:** takes off, climbs, cruises and lands on its own, plans a route around terrain and holds the highway centre line.\n- **Recovery:** after a rubberband, a disconnect or being sent to the lobby, it reconnects and carries on with the same route. It walks the trip back through the lobby portal and handles cracked-account `/login`.\n- **Safety logouts:** low elytra durability, low health (**minimum-health**, 4 hearts by default), lava, being stuck and inventory problems. A safety logout turns reconnect off.\n- **Lava and portals:** flies over or around lava where it safely can, and otherwise hands over to Baritone walking. Nether portals are crossed in a straight, checked line.\n- **Armour swapping:** can wear a chestplate while walking and put the elytra back on before takeoff.\n- **Discord webhooks:** sends trip start, arrival, disconnect, recovery, logout and status messages, with an optional mention and a test button.\n- **HUD elements:** **highway-fly-status** (phase, action and distance left) and **highway-fly-runtime** (active and total trip time).\n\n### Travel helpers\n\n**Anti Portal**, **Auto Set Home** and **Auto Lobby** are separate modules that you can use on their own. Highway Fly and Auto Boat Fly switch them on when a trip needs them.\n\n- **Auto Set Home:** learns the server's home cooldown and keeps it, along with its schedule and the last 100 confirmed homes, between sessions. A new **auto-set-home-timer** HUD element shows when the next `/sethome` will go out.\n- **Auto Lobby:** recognises the cracked lobby, the main lobby and the waiting area.\n\n### Boat Fly and Auto Boat Fly (new)\n\n- **Boat Fly:** a flying boat that passes through blocks, steered by hand with WASD, jump and sprint.\n- **Auto Boat Fly:** holds a fixed heading for AFK travel and works with AutoWalk, AutoEat, Auto Set Home and Auto Lobby. It has safety logouts for running out of eGaps, low health, lava, being dismounted and getting stuck. It also has a food watchdog and limits on how long reconnects keep trying.\n\n### Flight Dashboard (new)\n\nA read-only web page on your local network (default port **8734**) that shows Highway Fly and Auto Boat Fly trips live: phase, route progress, health, recovery state, an event feed and every setting, with passwords hidden. An access token can be set to protect it.\n\n### Comet Scaffold (new)\n\nAn independent scaffold with two presets. **Wide** fills the whole reachable strip and repairs holes. **Narrow** follows your sprint or sprint-jump path. Highway Fly pauses it and Meteor's Scaffold during a trip and turns them back on afterwards.\n\n### Chat Tools\n\n- **New window:** sized to your screen, with a sidebar for Overview, Players, Clan, Homes, Hotspot, Auto TPY and Settings. Every setting is in one place with a search box.\n- **Message queue:** Enter queues your messages, so typing never pauses, and \"please wait\" refusals are retried. A tray shows each waiting message with a countdown and a cancel button.\n- **Waiting for you:** teleport requests, unread messages and failed syncs are listed on Overview and shown as an in-game notification until you deal with them.\n- **Auto TPY:** accepts teleport requests at a pace you set and can learn the server's timing. Meteor friends go first, retries are queued, and there's a whitelist (with CSV import), a blocklist that always wins and a live queue view. You can also limit it to clan members with Discord roles you pick.\n\n### Discord IGN sync (new)\n\n\n..."
		},
