			"notes": "# Comet 0.25.20 — first public release\n\n**Comet** is a client-side [Meteor Client](https://meteorclient.com/) addon for Minecraft, built around movement, building, storage, chat and server-aware tooling. It is maintained as three parallel branches, and this is the first public release with builds for **26.1.2**, **26.2** and **1.21.11**.\n\n![Minecraft](https://img.shields.io/badge/Minecraft-26.1.2%20%7C%2026.2%20%7C%201.21.11-3c8527)\n![Meteor Client](https://img.shields.io/badge/Meteor%20Client-build%2042%20%7C%2035%20%7C%2082-8e44ad)\n![Licence](https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-GPL--3.0--only-blue)\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> All three builds share version **0.25.20** and the same feature set. Pick the build that matches your Minecraft version. The 26.1.2 branch is the default.\n\n## Downloads\n\n| Build | Minecraft | Java | Meteor Client | Mod JAR |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Default** | 26.1.2 | 25 | build 42 or newer | `comet-0.25.20-mc26.1.2.jar` |\n| **Latest MC** | 26.2 | 25 | build 35 or newer | `comet-0.25.20-mc26.2.jar` |\n| **Older servers** | 1.21.11 | 21 | build 82 or newer | `comet-0.25.20-mc1.21.11.jar` |\n\n**Which file do I need?**\n\n- **26.1.2** — use this by default, including on 26.1.x servers.\n- **26.2** — use this if you play on 26.2.\n- **1.21.11** — use this for 1.21.11 servers or older setups.\n\nEach JAR has a matching `-source.zip` attached for GPL compliance. Download the source archive only if you need to inspect, rebuild or redistribute Comet.\n\n## New in 0.25.20\n\n- **First public release** for all three Minecraft branches.\n- **Proxy tools** — fetch free SOCKS proxies, open clicked links in a proxy-bound browser profile, and open verification links directly or through the active proxy.\n- **Licensing cleanup** — one GPL-3.0-only `LICENSE` for the combined work, CC0 retained for original Comet code, and the Apache-2.0 text for the NoTextureRotations adaptation.\n- **Documentation and release tooling** — install steps, a supported-branch table, a contents list, new `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and CI builds for branches and `v*` tags.\n\n## What's included\n\n### Flight and movement\n\n- **Adaptive Elytra Fly** — vanilla-style elytra movement with terrain pacing, a setback-tolerant boost, an engine HUD and optional flight diagnostics.\n- **DEVILS Auto Wasp** — elytra pursuit with obstacle routing, path search, speed ramp, setback recovery and takeoff/landing handling.\n- **Baritone Elytra** — turns long `#goto` and `#path` trips into elytra flights when Meteor's Baritone is installed.\n- **Elytra Log** — disconnects safely when elytra durability gets low.\n- **Angle Calculator** — coordinate angle locking for building and travel.\n- **No Hurt Cam** — removes the camera shake on damage.\n\n### Chat and social\n\n- **Chat Tools** — a dedicated window for messages, player commands, homes, teleport timers, conversations, clan and friend management, recents and favourites.\n- **Call to Arms** — Discord webhook alerts for fights or events.\n- **Stash Report** — coordinate-free reports for sharing stashes.\n- **Anti Coords** — hides coordinates in chat and screenshots.\n\n### Storage, building and inventory\n\n- **Fast Storage ESP** — cached shader-based storage highlighting without per-frame block reads.\n- **Shulker Icons** — renders shulker contents in the inventory.\n- **Dub Counter** — counts nearby chests and tracks opened containers.\n- **Scaffold upgrade** — optimized placement, tower handling and a Comet settings dropdown inside Meteor's Scaffold.\n- **Inventory Tweaks, Auto Tool, Auto Weapon and Auto Replenish upgrades** — client-thread transfers, inventory-aware tool/weapon selection and container refill controls.\n- **Safe Fast Use** — fast item use without accidentally opening newly placed shulkers.\n- **Block Coat** — TNT surface coating with jump placement.\n- **Smart Sponge** — targeted sponge placement and cleanup.\n- **Speedmine** — faster mining with optional server-supported bedrock breaking.\n\n..."
